- shellcheck -s bash addon/run.sh has only the 24 SC2155 and one SC2164
  warnings already present on origin/main; this change adds no warning.

## Regression and wire coverage

- Discovery: only usable numeric musicMode metadata publishes the 0..100
  configuration slider; case variants and malformed/empty metadata are covered.
- Input: decimal values round, out-of-range values clamp, and NaN, infinity,
  overflow, and non-numeric MQTT payloads fail explicitly.
- Ordering: the real slider handler waits for the per-device control permit.
- MQTT: discovery and state echo share one topic constructor; exact topic,
  payload, reset of stale HA state after restart, and publish-error propagation
  are asserted.
- Platform API: sensitivity, historical defaults, clamping, autoColor, and one
  packed RGB colour are asserted in payload builders and through an in-process
  HTTP capture server.
- Home Assistant: a Music effect plus rgb_color disables autoColor on the wire;
  an ordinary scene in the same command ignores RGB as before.
- State: scene dispatch uses the fresh canonical sensitivity and retains the
  detached-device fallback without cloning full device/catalog state.
- Add-on: a source-level contract ties the schema option, translation, run
  script export, and exact environment variable consumed by the bridge.

